{
  "//": [
    "FOR THE TECHNICAL REVIEWER ONLY.",
    "",
    "Copy this to .claude/settings.local.json (git-ignored by Claude Code's own",
    "default ignore rules — verify with `git check-ignore .claude/settings.local.json`)",
    "to widen what you can do on your own machine.",
    "",
    "!! IMPORTANT — READ THIS BEFORE RELYING ON THE FILE !!",
    "",
    "A `deny` rule ALWAYS beats an `allow` rule, at every settings tier. An",
    "allow entry here CANNOT re-grant a path that .claude/settings.json denies.",
    "This was verified by execution: with both files in place, editing",
    "next.config.ts, app/globals.css, lib/config/nav.ts and",
    "components/booking/BookDemo.tsx all fail with",
    "'File is in a directory that is denied by your permission settings.'",
    "",
    "So the file-path allow entries below are INERT and kept only to document",
    "intent. What DOES still work are the Bash entries whose matching deny rule",
    "is narrower: settings.json denies `git checkout main` and `git checkout -b`,",
    "so `Bash(git checkout:*)` here still buys you `git checkout staging`; it",
    "denies `gh secret` and `gh api`, so `Bash(gh:*)` still buys you `gh pr`.",
    "Entries whose deny twin is equal or broader (aws, deploy.sh, sync:wp) are",
    "fully blocked and this file cannot unblock them.",
    "",
    "To genuinely edit a protected file, use one of:",
    "  - temporarily comment the relevant deny entry out of settings.json, or",
    "  - work from a clone that does not carry the project settings.json, or",
    "  - launch with `claude --dangerously-skip-permissions` (bypasses ALL rules,",
    "    including the ones protecting production — use deliberately).",
    "",
    "Leave the hooks alone — the format-and-typecheck hook is useful to everyone.",
    "",
    "Do not commit settings.local.json. If it were committed, every editor would",
    "silently inherit these entries and nothing would warn anyone.",
    "",
    "Note: only `Edit(path)` rules are evaluated for files — `Write(path)` rules",
    "are silently ignored by Claude Code. Never add a Write(...) rule here."
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Edit(./app/globals.css)",
      "Edit(./components/ui/**)",
      "Edit(./components/icons/iso-icons.tsx)",
      "Edit(./next.config.ts)",
      "Edit(./package.json)",
      "Edit(./tsconfig.json)",
      "Edit(./eslint.config.mjs)",
      "Edit(./app/layout.tsx)",
      "Edit(./lib/config/site.ts)",
      "Edit(./lib/config/nav.ts)",
      "Edit(./lib/config/legal.ts)",
      "Edit(./lib/seo.ts)",
      "Edit(./app/sitemap.ts)",
      "Edit(./app/robots.ts)",
      "Edit(./lib/content/**)",
      "Edit(./scripts/**)",
      "Edit(./lib/booking/**)",
      "Edit(./components/booking/**)",
      "Edit(./components/forms/**)",
      "Edit(./lib/hubspot.ts)",
      "Edit(./app/_unmounted/**)",
      "Edit(./infra/**)",
      "Edit(./.github/**)",
      "Edit(./.claude/**)",
      "Bash(git checkout:*)",
      "Bash(git branch:*)",
      "Bash(git merge:*)",
      "Bash(git push:*)",
      "Bash(aws:*)",
      "Bash(gh:*)",
      "Bash(./scripts/deploy.sh:*)",
      "Bash(pnpm sync:wp:*)"
    ]
  }
}
